<title>FRANCE: French election tightens in SOFRES poll.</title>
<headline>French election tightens in SOFRES poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an opinion poll of voters' intentions ahead of the May 25/June 1 two-round parliamentary election.</p>
<p>The telephone poll of 1,000 representative adults aged at least 18 was conducted by SOFRES on May 16 and 17 for TF1 television and made public on Saturday.</p>
<p>Of those polled, 18 percent did not give a voting intention.</p>
<p>			   percentage  projected seats in</p>
<p>			    of vote    National Assembly</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		2		0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		 10	    23-31</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left  28	   191-206 *</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists		  6		*</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR/UDF-other right    40	   316-341</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front	   13	     0-2</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Other			 1		0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p>(* SOFRES gives no separate figure for Ecologists. They are included in the total for Socialists and other left).</p>
<p>A previous SOFRES poll on May 9-10 gave the Socialists and allies plus the Ecologists a projected 162-185 seats, the Communists 21-28 seats and the RPR/UDF and allies 338-370 seats.</p>
</text>
